Z||000000||skitime||12-23-2000||09:25 AM||||I am reaching out to the Fiero community for help. I need to transport a Fiero from the Fort Wayne, Indiana area to Lancaster PA area. I live near the Manheim Auto Auction in PA which is the largest car auction in the US. I know hundreds of car carriers come here every week from all over the eastern US.  Hopefully someone know someone involved in car trasportation.  I would of course like to do this as inexpensive as possible. The car could be driven here if it was someone I could trust.  Any ideas????||||reg||5
Z||000001||StuGood||12-23-2000||11:16 PM||||I'll probably be in Fort Wayne sometime soon.  How far a trip is it to Lancaster?  What sort of shape is the Fiero in?<P>Oh, and how mad would you be, if I got lost on the way?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> J/K  ||||reg||5
